{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"c0","type":"claim","text":"In shared living, disputes about what an agreement meant are a standard vehicle for distributive grievance: parties who judge the overall load unfair contest the meaning of agreements they would honour under a fairer split. General observation about recurring chore conflict, not a fact about this flat.","scope":"recurring chore conflicts in shared households","grounds":"the source account itself reports persistence, heat, and one party now avoiding the conversations — which fits grievance-expressed-through-ambiguity at least as well as pure coordination failure"},{"id":"o1","type":"objection","text":"The headline conjecture presents rivals where there is likely a conjunction. Underspecification explains the form the disputes take but not their persistence and heat, which are what the material reports. If grievance runs through ambiguity, the charge-sheet repurposing the account lists as one contingent failure mode (r9) is not contingent at all: the grievance will express itself through whatever medium exists.","bearing":"cuts against the exclusivity of the account's central framing (r1 and body) and against r9's treatment of record-weaponisation as a risk to mitigate rather than the default path under the distributive reading; does not establish the account's conjecture is false, only that 'not primarily a fairness fight' is unearned","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r1","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r9","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r11"],"depends":["c0"]},{"id":"o2","type":"objection","text":"The sequencing is unjustified and the cheapest test of the untested hypothesis was never designed. The account admits (r11) it cannot tell whether the issue is distributive, yet runs the coordination trial first and places the 'different conversation' only in the conditional branch where its diagnosis was wrong. A one-to-two-week tally of who actually did what needs no consent, no system and no conversation, runs inside the same trial window, and can stay private. Its omission means the trial does all its diagnostic work on the form-hypothesis and none on the load-hypothesis — an asymmetry in the direction most comfortable for the asker to receive.","bearing":"cuts against the account's ordering and the claim that the trial 'doubles as a diagnostic'; a tally is compatible with every move the account proposes, so the objection mandates an addition rather than a removal","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r11","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r6"],"depends":["o1"]},{"id":"o3","type":"objection","text":"r3 and r5 are inconsistent about power. r3 grants proposal-only standing, yet r5 has the asker declare old disputed agreements off the table for all three and 'hold to it'. Declaring what is discussable is not a proposal; if any flatmate's grievance rests on the past, a unilateral clean slate reads as amnesty engineered by whoever the record would have disadvantaged. The defensible core is narrower: the asker may decline to defend their own past interpretations and may offer supersession, but cannot adjourn others' grievances. 'Cannot be reconstructed, only superseded' is also overstated, and the past is used as evidence for the diagnosis (r1's grounds) while ruled unreconstructable in the flat.","bearing":"cuts against r5 as stated; a narrower personal-refusal-plus-proposed-supersession version survives, so the objection mandates reformulation rather than abandonment","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r5","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r3"]},{"id":"o4","type":"objection","text":"Two failure modes the account names separately interact in a way it never traces. r9 worries the record could become a charge sheet; r7 gives silence an exit but only for schedule-based silence; r4 says the avoidance's cause is undetermined. Together: a persistent visible record with the friend's name, a task and a deadline documents non-performance in real time where memory used to be vague. If the avoidance is about anything other than scheduling, the board makes silence more, not less, legible as defiance and hands the others a running exhibit.","bearing":"cuts against r6 and r7's claimed consequence that the system gives silence somewhere to go besides defiance; that consequence holds only for schedule-driven silence and may invert for other-driven silence","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r6","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r7","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r9","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r4"]},{"id":"o5","type":"objection","text":"The asking is mis-specified. Every question proposed to the friend is a format question — ten minutes, or messages? — which reveals cost tolerance, not reason; r8's claim that the asking 'gathers information about why they avoid' holds only if the friend volunteers it. A person avoiding these conversations may be waiting to be asked a different question (what's wrong, what would make these worth having, what doesn't feel fair), and being asked only about logistics may confirm their sense that the real subject is being managed around. There is also a frame-function gap: the offer is framed as convenience while the account concedes the trial 'doubles as a diagnostic' of the friend, and no guidance is given for the friend's 'why are you really doing this?'.","bearing":"cuts against r8's stated consequence (information-gathering without diagnosis); the format question survives as a low-stakes opener, but not as the information-gathering instrument r8 claims it to be","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r8","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r4"]},{"id":"o6","type":"objection","text":"The trial cannot bear the epistemic weight of the closing claim that a failed trial is evidence the problem was 'never about the form of the agreements at all'. A null result is evidence against the form-hypothesis only conditional on adequate implementation, genuine uptake by all three, and sufficient duration — none ensured: the record may be run in the distrust key (r9), upkeep may fall on one person (r10), the friend may never engage, and two weeks is short for a new coordination habit to displace an entrenched conflict pattern even when the diagnosis is right. Symmetrically, a calm fortnight may be novelty. The trial is a reasonable intervention and an unreliable instrument, and the account conflates the two.","bearing":"cuts against the body's final inference; the trial remains worth running, but its reading must stay confound-aware in both directions","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r6","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r9","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r10"]},{"id":"o7","type":"objection","text":"There is no branch for non-uptake, and the all-or-nothing framing converts the avoidant friend into an effective veto-holder. Every move presupposes the friend will at least entertain a format; the described avoidance makes non-engagement a live and likely outcome the account leaves unaddressed. r3's 'a system only works if offered as something the others can accept' also overlooks that with three residents, the asker plus the willing friend are a working majority for their own arrangements: a partial record covering two of three, third party invited and never compelled, lowers stakes and leaves the offer open without depending on the person least likely to accept it.","bearing":"cuts against r3's framing and r6's implied unanimity requirement; does not claim partial coordination should replace the full offer, only that it is an available fallback the account omits","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r3","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r6","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r8"]},{"id":"o8","type":"objection","text":"The account never considers that the asker might be the problem party. r11 asks whether one person in fact does much more, but the possibility that this person is the asker is never raised; no move has the asker solicit feedback about their own conduct; the questions proposed to the others concern format and tolerance, never what they wish the asker did differently. Self-report is systematically charitable to the reporter. If the asker is the under-contributor or the over-policer, the facilitator-designer role the account assigns them is tactically convenient, and the designer's sense of what counts as 'done' quietly sets the terms.","bearing":"cuts against the completeness of the account's failure-mode list; the remedy costs one line — track the asker's own items on the same record and invite the other two to flag them — and requires abandoning no other move","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r11","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r8","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r6"]},{"id":"u0","type":"use","text":"Proposed revision of the account's program, keeping its register (propose, don't enforce; ask, don't diagnose) and its record-trial: (a) run a silent load tally inside the same trial window; (b) replace the unilateral clean-slate declaration with a personal refusal to relitigate one's own past interpretations plus a proposed supersession; (c) add the asker's own items to the record with an explicit invitation to the other two to flag them; (d) add one substantive question to the re-approach (what would make these conversations worth having) alongside the format question; (e) pre-commit a two-of-three fallback if the avoidant friend declines every format.","scope":"the three flatmates' chore coordination and the asker's next steps","action":"amend the account's five moves as listed before proposing them to the flatmates","consequence":"the program tests both live hypotheses at once, avoids the unilateral-adjournment reading, and no longer grants the avoidant friend a veto over the asker's coordination with the third flatmate","depends":["o1","o2","o3","o5","o7","o8"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r5","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r6","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r8"]},{"id":"p0","type":"problem","text":"Whether the friend's avoidance tracks the cost of the conversations (the account's operating assumption) or their content is undetermined by the material. o4 and o5 presuppose the content-based possibility without establishing it; the friend's response, or non-response, to any offered format would only partially discriminate between the readings.","target":["h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r4"],"mentions":["o4","o5"]},{"id":"p1","type":"problem","text":"Calibration of my own criticism: o1's supporting generalisation — that pure coordination failure produces irritation and workarounds rather than topic-avoidance — is unverifiable from here. If it is false, sustained unwinnable memory-disputes may be aversive enough to produce avoidance on their own, o1 loses its abductive edge and reduces to the weaker but still standing claim that the exclusivity of the account's framing is unearned.","target":["o1"],"mentions":["c0"]}],"uptake":["c0","o1","o2","o3","o4","o5","o6","o7","o8","u0","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r9","h005.fork5.p.objection.0#r11"]}